# Rust
/target/
Cargo.log
**/*.rs.bk

# Tauri
.tauri/
# mcp-server-ts/build/ is intentionally COMMITTED (vendored): the MCP server
# consumed at runtime is this fork's build, pointed to by .mcp.json. Like dist-js
# below, the compiled artifact must be present in the tree so a fresh clone works
# without a build step. node_modules/ stays ignored (line below). Rebuild with
# `pnpm --dir mcp-server-ts build` (tsc) after editing mcp-server-ts/src/.
# dist-js/ is intentionally COMMITTED: this fork is consumed by ori/iwe apps via
# a pnpm `link:` path dependency. pnpm does NOT run lifecycle scripts (prepare)
# for linked local packages, so the compiled guest-js artifact must already be
# present in the tree — otherwise a fresh clone would leave a dead link with no
# dist-js to resolve. Rebuild with `pnpm build` after editing guest-js/.
# Re-include the dist-js type declaration: the parent ori/.gitignore excludes
# *.d.ts globally, but this vendored artifact must be tracked for type-checking.
!dist-js/*.d.ts
